      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Since the removal of particle drivers in child animators (which broke a bunch of features I had on my avatars) I've been struggling to get motivation to get in unity and create more stuff. It was the base block for a lot of things I had. I don't want to go back to the pre SDK 3.0 era way of doing things with mega hacks, dropping performance, and not being able to synchronize stuff.\nThis should be a very light weight and simple solution that opens so many doors in avatar creation. It sucks having hands tied, this might not be usable directly by every avatar creator, but fortunately there are a ton of people that make prefab systems and tutorials that enables beginner avatar creators to take advantage of it.\nI am sorry for this little rant, but I really wouldn't like something like this to fall in oblivion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
